{
  "_comment": [
    "Device profiles for screen-capture shot ingestion (ADR-014).",
    "A profile is the *only* device-specific thing in the pipeline: it names the tile",
    "labels to look for, which ShotData field each one feeds, and how to read the sign",
    "off the qualifier the device prints next to the number. No pixel coordinates —",
    "the parser locates cells geometrically, so a profile survives a different photo",
    "framing, screen size, or crop.",
    "Fields with target=null are boundary-only: they are not stored, but finding them",
    "keeps the neighbouring cell from spilling into their column."
  ],
  "profiles": [
    {
      "device": "hd_golf",
      "title": "SHOT DATA",
      "value_span_ratio": 3.5,
      "blank_markers": ["---", "--", "—", "- - -"],
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Shot Distance",
          "target": "total_distance",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "yards"
        },
        {
          "label": "Carry",
          "target": "carry_distance",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "yards"
        },
        {
          "label": "Bounce & Roll",
          "aliases": ["Bounce Roll", "Bounce and Roll"],
          "target": "bounce_and_roll",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "yards"
        },
        {
          "label": "Ball Speed",
          "target": "ball_speed",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "mph"
        },
        {
          "label": "Launch Angle",
          "target": "launch_angle",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees"
        },
        {
          "label": "Club Speed",
          "target": "club_head_speed",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "mph"
        },
        {
          "label": "Club Path",
          "target": "club_path",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["I>O", "I O", "IO", "1>0", "I>0"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["O>I", "O I", "OI", "0>1", "O>1"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Custom",
          "target": null,
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "label": "Club Face Angle",
          "target": "club_face_angle",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["OPEN"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["CLOSED", "CLOSE"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Spin",
          "target": "spin_rate",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "rpm"
        },
        {
          "label": "Smash Factor",
          "target": "smash_factor",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "ratio"
        },
        {
          "label": "Impact Position",
          "target": "impact_position",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "label": "Shot Type",
          "target": "shot_type",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "label": "Horizontal Angle",
          "target": "launch_direction",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["R", "RIGHT"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["L", "LEFT"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_comment": [
            "The one tile HD Golf prints already signed ('-9.3 °'), and its polarity is the",
            "opposite of the ShotData contract's (+ = fade). Both real shots on disk print a",
            "negative axis while the screen's own Shot Type tile beside them reads FADE, and",
            "on both the face sits >10 ° open to the path, which curves the ball right for",
            "this right-handed golfer. Three readings of one screen agreeing, so printed_sign",
            "is -1 rather than a guess. validate.py cross-checks the stored sign against Shot",
            "Type on every parse, so if this is ever wrong for some shot shape it says so",
            "instead of quietly storing a fade as a draw.",
            "sign_tokens stays: if HD Golf ever prints '9.3 ° R', the word still wins."
          ],
          "label": "Spin Axis",
          "target": "spin_axis",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "printed_sign": -1,
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["R", "RIGHT"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["L", "LEFT"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
